DESCRIPTION:Over the past two decades\, Nick Paumgarten has become one of 
 The New Yorker’s most admired staff writers. His long-awaited first book
 \, a memoir\, uses his consuming lifelong obsession with hockey as a prism
  into a deeply entertaining exploration of the game’s tribe and its unre
 asonable demands.\nNick will be joined in conversation by Chris Jennings\,
  the author of Paradise Now: The Story of American Utopianism.\n****\nABOU
 T THIS EVENT\nThis event will be hosted by Book Passage at our SF Ferry Bu
 ilding store.\nFree Admission / Open Seating\nFollowing the presentation\,
  there will be a signing line or a meet-and-greet.\nIf you are unable to a
 ttend the event\, you can still get your copy by clicking the "BUY THE BOO
 K" button above. If you would like a signed or personalized book\, please 
 note that in the order comment field.\nFor any questions regarding our eve
 nts\, please contact us at books@bookpassage.com.\n\nFree\nBook Passage Pr
 esents:\n\nTickets: https://bookpassage.com/event/nick-paumgarten-intangib
 les\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/16/nick-paumgarten-with-
 chris-jennings-the-intangibles-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
