UID:funcheap-1644988@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Community
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSF YIMBYSan Francisco’s Fami
 ly Zoning Plan turned back decades of exclusionary zoning and is expected 
 to generate meaningfully more housing for the city\, but it still isn’t 
 enough to meet the state’s mandated housing targets. Join us on Wednesda
 y\, November 18th at the Eureka Valley Rec Center\, where housing activist
  Robert Fruchtman will explain the “circuit breaker” built into the Fa
 mily Zoning Plan to ensure the city hits its housing goals.\nYou’ll lear
 n what San Francisco promised the state\, and what additional zoning and p
 olicy changes might be needed to get there. Join us to learn more about so
 lving SF’s housing affordability crisis.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www
 .zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/circuit-breaker-101-learn-how-and-why-sf-will-n
 eed-to-upzone-again-in-2027-copy\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-ta
 lk-sf-housing-101-upzoning-return-2027/\nSource: Funcheap SF
