SUMMARY:3rd Saturday Poetry in Chinatown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
DTSTAMP:20261118T115305Z
UID:funcheap-1645911@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerClarion Performing Arts Center
 Open mic before and after the featured poets. Sign up at 3 pm.\n\nJessica 
 Loos is best known for her improvisational performances with music\, inclu
 ding collaborations with Marco Eneidi\, Cecil Taylor\, Drop D\, Mario Saca
 sa\, and many others. She plays the tambourine and also makes collages. 
 ◦ She grew up in New Jersey\, went to University of Maine\, Orono\, and 
 had a wild run in the Lower East Side of Manhattan\, where she became a me
 mber of The Living Theatre and a contributing writer for High Times magazi
 ne. She has an MA/MFA from New College of California. She also taught ther
 e\, as well as at Academy of Art University. Her latest collection\, Tambo
 urine\, was published by Lithic Press in April 2026. She lives in San Fran
 cisco where she organizes poetry and music events.\n\nClara Hsu is a Chine
 se-American poet and executive director of Clarion Performing Arts Center 
 in San Francisco Chinatown. Her bi-lingual music video\, Gai Mou Sou Rap\,
  went viral on the internet. Clara has also written two plays in the Canto
 nese language: DragonBeard (2024) and A Lantern Riddle (2026) to spark int
 erest and uplift the spirit of Cantonese Americans. Visit clarahsu.com\n\n
 Parking tip:\n$8 all-day parking at St. Mary’s Square Garage.\n\nFree\n\
 nTickets: https://www.theclarionsf.org/events/3rd-saturday-poetry-in-china
 town-42\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/3rd-saturday-poetry-chinatown-19
 /\nSource: Funcheap SF
