 nd Marine tugboat Saturday\, November 28\, for photos and festivities. Arr
 ive at 11:30 am with your family and friends to enjoy live entertainment f
 rom the Pacific Empire Chorus while waiting for Santa and Mrs. Claus to ar
 rive! By noon\, the couple will disembark at the Turning Basin. Young Nutc
 racker-costumed dancers from Petaluma School of Ballet will escort the cou
 ple to their special holiday tent adjacent to Taps on the River for photos
  with eager children. The jolly pair will leave at 1:30 pm for their next 
 stop on their holiday tour.\nNovember 28 is also Shop Small Saturday. As y
 ou queue up for photos\, grab a Shop Small bag filled with items from loca
 l merchants\, while supply lasts. Bring your holiday shopping lists and su
 pport local! Historic downtown\, filled with boutiques from chic to quirky
  and fortifying farm-to-table dining and tasting rooms\, is just a couple 
 blocks away. The kids will love spotting Holiday Hen Hunt chickens in shop
  windows to fill their bingo cards for a chance to win prizes!\nIf you’r
 e coming from out of town\, the festivities are just three blocks from the
  Petaluma Downtown Smart Station\, so you can skip the parking and the tra
 ffic\, while doing a solid for the planet.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://pet
 alumadowntown.com/santa-riverboat-arrival\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.co
 m/santas-riverboat-arrival-shop-small-saturday-petaluma/\nSource: Funcheap
