 clude train rides\, face painting\, balloon artistry\, and free treat bags
  (while supplies last). With a warm\, welcoming atmosphere\, the event is 
 designed to create lasting memories for families and friends.\nWhen: Sunda
 y\, November 29\, from 6:00 – 8:00 pm\n\nWhere: Pacific Commons Shopping
  Center\n43440 Boscell Road\nFremont\, CA 94538\n(near Market Broiler)\nAb
 out Pacific Commons\nPacific Commons is a dominant\, regional power center
  located off the I-880 corridor in the middle of Silicon Valley. This 1.1 
 million square-foot shopping destination is home to such popular retailers
  as Target\, Burlington\, Lowe’s\, Costco\, Nordstrom Rack\, DSW\, Old N
 avy\, T.J. Maxx/HomeGoods\, Ulta Beauty\, Total Wine & More\, Men’s Wear
 house and Century Theatres. Restaurant tenants include The Kebab Shop\, Ma
 rket Broiler\, KoJa Kitchen\, and more.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://pacifi
 ccommons.com/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-annual-holiday-tree-l
