DESCRIPTION:SF’s GLBT History Museum: Free First Wednesday\nGLBT History
  Museum\nLocated in SF’s Castro District\, the GLBT Historical Society M
 useum is the first full-scale\, stand-alone museum of its kind in the Unit
 ed States. The museum celebrates 100 years of the city’s vast queer past
  through dynamic exhibitions and programming.\nNormally\, admission is $10
 \, but on the first Wednesday of every month\, admission is free for every
 one\, thanks to a grant from the Bob Ross Foundation. Free tickets are not
  available for reservation online on free days\; all visitors will be welc
 omed to the museum as long as there is capacity on a first-come\, first-se
 rved basis.\nThere’s also free admission for children 12 and under\, plu
 s SNAP EBT and Medi-Cal cardholders: Free + 3 guests. Supplemental Nutriti
 on Assistance Program (SNAP) cardholders receive free admission through Mu
 seums for All. Cardholders may present their card and valid ID to receive 
 free admission. To reserve advance tickets\, contact tickets@glbthistory.o
 rg.\n\nGLBT History Museum Hours\nTuesday–Sunday: 11:00 a.m.–1:00 p.m.
  and 1:30 p.m.–5:00 p.m.\nMonday: Closed\n– Updated 1/8/26 – Event i
 nfo last checked via website\n\nDiscounted Admission Programs\nDiscounted 
 admission: $6\nAvailable to youth (ages 13–17)\, seniors (age 65 and ove
 r)\, students and teachers (with ID)\, active-duty military service member
 s (with ID) and people with disabilities.\nGroups (10 or more people): Ple
 ase click here.\nDiscounted tickets are available for large groups booked 
 at lea...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.glbthistory.org/museum-about-vis
 itor-info\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-glbt-history-museum-free-f
 irst-wednesday-49/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/Museum
 _Main_Gallery_2016-06.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:GLBT Historical Society Museum\, 4127 18th St. San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-glbt-history-museum-free-first-wednesday-4
 9/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Admission Day at Yerba Buena Center for the Arts (YBCA)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T170000
DTSTAMP:20261008T104232Z
UID:funcheap-1641651@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerFree Admission Day at Yerba Bu
 ena Center for the Arts (YBCA)\nYerba Buena Center for the Arts\nOpened to
  the public in 1993\, YBCA was founded as the cultural anchor of San Franc
 isco’s Yerba Buena Gardens neighborhood. Our work spans the realms of co
 ntemporary art\, performance\, film\, civic engagement\, and public life. 
 Centering artists as essential to social and cultural movement\, YBCA is r
 eimagining the role an arts institution can play in the community it serve
 s.\nYBCA is located in the heart of San Francisco’s SOMA neighborhood\, 
 across the street from SFMOMA and the Moscone Convention Center. The main 
 entrance to our galleries and forum event space is at 701 Mission Street. 
 The main entrance to our theater is 700 Howard Street.\n\nYBCA is open Wed
 nesday–Sunday\, 11–5pm.\nEntry to YBCA Galleries is free every Wednesd
 ay\nTicketing\nGalleries\nMembers: Free\nAdult (18+): $10\nStudents & Seni
 ors: $5\nYouth (17 and under)\, Military Personnel\, & Museums for All: Fr
 ee\nWednesdays: Free\nEmployees of other museums with current valid staff 
 ID receive free general admission for themselves and one guest.\nMuseums f
 or All\nYBCA offers free admission for Medi-Cal and EBT card holders as pa
 rt of the Museums for All program. Benefits card required upon entry. Tick
 ets must be purchased at the ticketing desk at YBCA.\nHours\nGalleries\nWe
