SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Community
DESCRIPTION:Museum of the Game\n​Can love be measured? For over a hundre
 d years\, we have been on a quest to measure love and uncover the principl
 es of romantic affection. . .\n\n​This month\, we’re reading “Love T
 ester Machines\,” a history of devices that promised to predict whether 
 two people were a match. To see how they worked firsthand\, we’re taking
  Gray Area book club offsite for the first time\, to the Musée Mécanique
 \, the largest museum of arcades in the US.\n\nBring your friend\, partner
 \, or check your compatibility with another book club regular! At the end 
 of the day\, it’s just a gamble . . .or not?\n\nDecember 20\, 2026\nTime
 : 12–2 PM\nMusée Mécanique\, Pier 45\, San Francisco\, CA 94133\nRSVP 
 https://luma.com/757om85p\n\nLogistics: To operate the machines\, you need
  quarters\; there’s an on-site ATM. Admission to the museum is free.\n\n
 Free\n\nTickets: https://luma.com/757om85p\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.c
 om/cybersentics-book-club-love-testers-muse-mcanique-tour-sf/\nSource: Fun
 cheap SF
